  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe post-merge gate on main is red (runs 44279917425 and 44285991575). This PR fixes each cause. No assert is relaxed and no refusal is made wider. The reasons are in `docs/decisions/2483-main-red-fixtures.md`.\n\n1. `microarc_test_part::a_wrapped_op_on_the_test_part_posts_wrapped_a`\n   - Cause: commit 8f99bcb4c (Refs #419, merged with #468) changed `arc_chords` in `crates/cl/src/cl/moves.rs`. When the two radii differ (`ra != rb`), the step also obeys a curvature bound. One turning arc of the test part has radii that differ in the last float digits. It now posts 8 chords, not 7. #2386 made the golden on a base before that commit.\n   - Fix: one hunk of `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/tormach/wrap_rotary_parallel_microarc4.nc` (old lines 1326-1332) takes the 8 new lines. The rest of the golden does not change, so no Windows last-digit rounding enters it.\n   - The new chords stay inside the chord tolerance. The end points and the end A do not change. The exact float compare is filed as #2520 (P7).\n2. `stock_source_holes::framed_stock_chamfer_live_refusal_keeps_hint_without_local_move_number`\n   - Cause: #2450 (49c268ba7) added the #2435 wall law. With a 10-degree tilt, the ride plane at the stock top (Z20) crosses the top face along a line that is no edge. The law refuses that line by name. The refusal is correct: a cone on that line cuts a groove, not a chamfer.\n   - Fix: the fixture rides at mid-wall (`MID = 10.0`, `crates/app/tests/stock_source_holes.rs` near line 252). The added part's top moves with it. The asserts do not change. The test reaches the live refusal that it pins again.\n   - The refusal says \"into the part\" also for a stock source. Filed as #2521 (P7, wording).\n3. `guide_projects::demo_projects_build_and_load_with_valid_paths` (`camcraft-ui` lib): passes on 2c789ed6d (after #2499). No change.\n4. Clippy: after #2488, `crates/app/src/operation/heights.rs:128` fails `needless_borrows_for_generic_args`. The batch tier runs clippy. `.map(&resolve)` becomes `.map(resolve)`. No behaviour change.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate test a_wrapped_op_on_the_test_part_posts_wrapped_a --crate camcraft-app --binary microarc_test_part`: ok.\n- `cargo xtask gate test framed_stock_chamfer_live_refusal_keeps_hint_without_local_move_number --crate camcraft-app --binary stock_source_holes`: ok.\n- Full suites `microarc_test_part` (4 passed), `stock_source_holes` (9 passed), `heights_selection` (9 passed).\n- `camcraft-app` lib unit tests: 367 passed (before the one-token clippy edit).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --lib --test microarc_test_part --test stock_source_holes -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` selects every `camcraft-app` suite, because a golden file is a shared test input. Only `microarc_test_part.rs` reads this golden. I stopped that run after the lib and three suites passed, and ran the touched suites by name.\n- Clippy `--all-targets` for the whole crate, and the other crates.\n- The post-merge batch gate. It runs on main after the merge, and its next green run also closes #2483.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFixes #2483\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
